/*
  Cache-Control for the Mini App static assets.

  Root cause of the "new HTML, old CSS" bug: Cloudflare Pages serves
  /styles/main.css and /scripts/app.js at the same URL on every
  deploy (filenames aren't content-hashed), so browsers and
  Cloudflare's own edge cache can keep serving a stale copy after a
  new deploy - which is exactly what happened (metallic plate/rivet/
  icon-sizing rules never loaded, leaving unstyled SVGs and flat
  fallback colors from an earlier commit). no-cache forces a
  revalidation request on every load instead of serving a cached copy
  blindly.
*/
/styles/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/scripts/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
